  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1239 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nA more zonal pattern looks to follow in the wake of the passing\nupper-level trough Saturday with most models still holding on to\nsome breezy conditions Sunday. Temperatures are expected to stay\ncooler for the day as well with afternoon high temperatures only\nexpected to reach into the 50s. However by Monday, drier\nconditions alongside down-sloping southwesterly winds should allow\nthe Panhandles to warm back into the 60s. These conditions do look\nto last through Tuesday and most of Wednesday with locations also\nlooking to hold in the 60s as well. By next Thursday, present\nmodels have continued to trend towards another upper-level closed\nlow pushing in from Southern California and moving across the\nSouthern Great Plains. However, models are still struggling with\nits exact path and strength, which has confidence down at this\ntime. For now present ensembles have given the Panhandles around a\n10 to 30 percent chances of seeing any precipitation. Otherwise,\nlook for temperatures to cool with this passage with highs in the\n50s looking close out the work week. &&",
